Title: Financial Inclusion in Latin America: Facts and Obstacles - Working Paper 439
Abstract: This paper shows that, in spite of recent progress in the usage of alternative financial services by
adult populations, Latin America’s financial inclusion gaps relative to either high-income countries
or the region’s comparators (countries with a similar degree of development) have not reduced
generally and, in some cases, have even increased during the period 2011-2014. 
